---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { parse } from 'yaml';
import { marked } from 'marked';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Principle from '../components/Principle.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const manifesto = parse(readFileSync('src/data/manifesto.yaml', 'utf-8'));
const romanNumerals = ['I', 'II', 'III', 'IV', 'V', 'VI', 'VII', 'VIII'];

// Parse all principle descriptions as inline markdown
for (const section of manifesto.sections) {
  for (const p of section.principles) {
    p.description = await marked.parseInline(p.description.trim());
  }
}
---

<Layout title="rewrites.bio - Rewrite it, for bioinformatics">
  <Hero />

  <main class="manifesto">
    <div class="preamble container reveal-stagger">
      <p class="reveal">
        Many of our most trusted tools were written years ago, when datasets were orders
        of magnitude smaller. They work correctly. They are thoroughly validated. They are
        also slow, dependency-heavy, and expensive to run at modern sequencing scale.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal">
        Tools that were fast enough ten years ago are now a bottleneck: in time, in
        cost, and in environmental impact. Rewrites that cut runtimes, reduce dependencies,
        and lower resource consumption are not just nice to have. At modern scale, they are
        becoming essential.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal">
        AI coding assistants have changed the equation. A domain expert can now rewrite
        established tools in compiled languages in days, not years. Fast code has become
        cheap. The scientific insight, careful validation, and community trust behind the
        original tools have not.
      </p>
      <p class="preamble-callout reveal">
        A wave of AI-assisted rewrites is coming.<br />
        The question is not <em>whether</em> it will happen, but whether it will happen <em>well</em>.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal">
        These are the principles we follow.
      </p>
    </div>

    {manifesto.sections.map((section: any, si: number) => (
      <Section id={section.title.toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, '-')} number={romanNumerals[si]} title={section.title}>
        {section.principles.map((p: any, pi: number) => (
          <Principle number={`${si + 1}.${pi + 1}`} title={p.title} description={p.description} />
        ))}
      </Section>
    ))}

    <section class="closing container">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="closing-line"></div>
        <p class="closing-text">
          The wave is coming.<br />
          Let us make sure it lifts all boats.
        </p>
        <p class="closing-attribution">
          {/* Read the paper: <em>The Bioinformatics Rewrite</em> (preprint coming soon)<br /> */}
          Plain text version: <a href="/manifesto.md"><code>rewrites.bio/manifesto.md</code></a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .manifesto {
    padding-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .preamble {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .preamble p {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    max-width: 65ch;
  }

  .preamble-callout {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.05rem !important;
    color: var(--rust-400) !important;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--rust-600);
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
    margin: var(--space-xl) 0 !important;
    line-height: 1.8 !important;
  }

  .preamble-callout em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--rust-300);
  }

  .closing {
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .closing-line {
    width: 48px;
    height: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--rust-600), var(--rust-400));
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-xl);
  }

  .closing-text {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.5vw, 1.6rem);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .closing-text a {
    color: inherit;
  }
  .closing-text a:hover {
    color: var(--rust-400);
  }

  .closing-attribution {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .closing-attribution a {
    color: inherit;
  }
  .closing-attribution a:hover {
    color: var(--rust-400);
  }

</style>
